{{- /* Workspace-only commit-signing key. Coder pods must sign commits (protected
branches require signatures) without holding a key that can authenticate as the human,
so this key is registered on GitHub as a signing key only -- signing-type keys carry no
SSH authentication capability -- while the personal authentication key never renders on
pods (see .chezmoiignore). While the Bitwarden secret id below is an unfilled
placeholder, the guard skips the lookup and this renders empty; chezmoi creates no file
from empty contents, so the gitconfig's stat guard leaves signing unconfigured instead
of the whole apply failing on an unresolvable secret id. */ -}}
{{- $uuid := "<<TODO-github-ppat-workspacesigningkey-uuid>>" -}}
{{- if not (hasPrefix "<<TODO" $uuid) -}}
{{ (bitwardenSecrets $uuid .bwsAccessToken).value }}
{{ end -}}
